{"id":"leandros","name":"Leandros","type":"character","aliases":[],"description":"An Akroan warrior of the Alamon who patrols Akros's perimeter and is sole survivor of his squad.","pages":2,"first_seen":"2014-02-26","last_seen":"2014-02-26","description_citations":[{"source":"mtg-wiki","official":false,"publisher":"MTG Wiki contributors","work":"Leandros","series":"MTG Wiki","authors":[],"date":"","url":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Leandros","link":"https://mtg.wiki/page/Leandros","archived":null,"license":"CC BY-NC-SA 4.0","text":"\"Leandros\". MTG Wiki contributors, CC BY-NC-SA 4.0."}],"bio":null,"timeline":[{"id":"walls-akros-2014-02-26-e0","era":null,"summary":"Ten soldiers of the Alamon wait at the Horns for Eumalos's squad, and Captain Kyrillos sends Bardas and Borias to climb the stones.","participants":["captain-kyrillos","leandros","bardas","borias","the-alamon"],"location":"the-horns-of-nicol-bolas","importance":"minor","page":"stories/walls-akros-2014-02-26","order":432,"story_date":"2014-02-26","storyline":"Born of the Gods","source":"wizards","paragraph":14,"quote":"Bardas, Borias—climb the Horns and see what you can see.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26#:~:text=Bardas%2C%20Borias%E2%80%94climb%20the%20Horns,what%20you%20can%20see.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Walls of Akros","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kelly Digges"],"date":"2014-02-26","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26#:~:text=Bardas%2C%20Borias%E2%80%94climb%20the%20Horns,what%20you%20can%20see.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Walls of Akros\" by Kelly Digges. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 26 Feb 2014."}},{"id":"walls-akros-2014-02-26-e1","era":null,"summary":"A wounded cyclops attacks the squad; Pallas is backhanded, and the squad kills it with Mnesos's sling and Nikasios's spear.","participants":["pallas","mnesos","nikasios","leandros","bardas","borias"],"location":"the-horns-of-nicol-bolas","importance":"minor","page":"stories/walls-akros-2014-02-26","order":432,"story_date":"2014-02-26","storyline":"Born of the Gods","source":"wizards","paragraph":34,"quote":"There was a crack as Mnesos's stone met the cyclops's skull, and the creature roared.","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26#:~:text=There%20was%20a%20crack,and%20the%20creature%20roared.","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Walls of Akros","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kelly Digges"],"date":"2014-02-26","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26#:~:text=There%20was%20a%20crack,and%20the%20creature%20roared.","archived":null,"license":null,"text":"\"The Walls of Akros\" by Kelly Digges. Magic Story, Wizards of the Coast, 26 Feb 2014."}},{"id":"walls-akros-2014-02-26-e3","era":null,"summary":"At night Leandros asks Mnesos why the gods have abandoned them and whether they will return; Mnesos says the gods have retreated into Nyx before.","participants":["leandros","mnesos","nyx"],"location":"theros","importance":"minor","page":"stories/walls-akros-2014-02-26","order":432,"story_date":"2014-02-26","storyline":"Born of the Gods","source":"wizards","paragraph":64,"quote":"The historians tell us that this is not the first time the gods have retreated into Nyx","link":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26#:~:text=The%20historians%20tell%20us,have%20retreated%20into%20Nyx","citation":{"source":"wizards","official":true,"publisher":"Wizards of the Coast","work":"The Walls of Akros","series":"Magic Story","authors":["Kelly Digges"],"date":"2014-02-26","url":"https://magic.wizards.com/en/news/magic-story/walls-akros-2014-02-26